    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "It starts with sunlight! Sunlight looks white, but it's really all the colours of the rainbow mixed together.",
      "punch": "rainbow",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "☀️",
        "text": "Sunlight = all colours",
        "cue": "sunlight",
        "sub": "Mixed together!",
        "sub_cue": "mixed"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "All the colours? Even blue?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Yes! When sunlight zooms into our air, it bumps into teeny tiny bits of air, much too small to see.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "💨",
        "text": "Light bumps into air",
        "cue": "bumps",
        "sub": "Tiny, tiny bits",
        "sub_cue": "tiny"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Blue light gets bounced all over the sky, much more than red or yellow light, which mostly go straight.",
      "punch": "bounced",
      "board": {
        "type": "compare",
        "left": {
          "label": "Blue",
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Bounces a lot",
              "icon": "🔵",
              "cue": "blue"
            },
            {
              "text": "All over the sky",
              "icon": "💫",
              "cue": "sky"
            }
          ]
        },
        "right": {
          "label": "Red & yellow",
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Red: straight",
              "icon": "🔴",
              "cue": "red"
            },
            {
              "text": "Yellow: straight",
              "icon": "🟡",
              "cue": "yellow"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "So when I look up, blue light is coming from everywhere?",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "👀",
        "text": "Blue from everywhere!",
        "cue": "everywhere"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Exactly! That's why a clear, sunny day looks so blue."
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Then why does the sky turn orange at sunset?",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🌅",
        "text": "Orange sunset?",
        "cue": "sunset"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "At sunset, sunlight travels through lots more air to reach you. The blue gets scattered away, so reds and oranges are left.",
      "board": {
        "type": "steps",
        "title": "At sunset",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": "Light takes a long trip",
            "icon": "🛤️",
            "cue": "travels"
          },
          {
            "label": "Blue scatters away",
            "icon": "🔵",
            "cue": "scattered"
          },
          {
            "label": "Reds and oranges left",
            "icon": "🟠",
            "cue": "reds"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "So sunlight has every colour, blue bounces the most, and at sunset the reds win!",
      "board": {
        "type": "summary",
        "rows": [
